-- title:
--   Finiteness of the Γ₀(M') level automorphisms, case q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 3$, let $M' \geq 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, subject to the hypothesis that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $q^2M'$ and group $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that field of $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansions, $H$ being the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Finally let $\tau : \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \to \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ be any map such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism $\tau(\gamma)$ satisfies [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) for the data $(L, q, \zeta, q, q^2M', H, \gamma^{-1}, K)$: that is, for all $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, all weight-$k$ modular forms $f, g$ for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansion power series $p_f, p_g$ and $p_g$ giving a nonzero Laurent series, every $x \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is the image of $p_f/p_g$ under the coefficient embedding $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = \exp(2\pi i/q)$, one has $\iota_*(\tau(\gamma)x) \cdot q\text{-exp}(g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}) = q\text{-exp}(f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\delta$ is the determinant-one matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\delta = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}$. The conclusion is that there is a subgroup $G \leq \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ which is finite and whose elements are exactly the $\tau(\gamma)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   This records that the level automorphisms of $K/L$ attached to the elements of $\Gamma_0(M')$ close up into a finite subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$, so that $K$ is a finite Galois-type extension of the fixed field and descent arguments for the covering of modular function fields apply. It is the $q = 3$ form of the statement, used in the analysis of the comparison of places, ramification index one and separability over the Gauss–$\Gamma_0$ situation for $X_H$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_subgroup_finite_mem_iff_exists_eq_of_isLevelAutAt_of_eq_three.lean

